## Lore

The Brodkil are towering sub-demons that came through the Rifts: nine or ten
feet of mega-damage muscle with strength and stamina beyond anything mortal,
and the knack of vanishing from sight whenever they please. Beyond that they
have little that is uncanny about them, no sorcery and no powers of the mind.

They build nothing and keep no nation. Tribes of a few dozen wander the
wilds as scavengers, and smaller war parties break off to rob travelers,
farms and towns, as glad to eat the people as the cattle. In the Pecos badlands
they ride with bandit gangs and favor the company of other big, vicious
creatures. They are bullies to the weak and quick to run from anything
stronger, fierce but never reckless, and cruel more from appetite than from
any taste for torment.

A Brodkil learns what helps it fight or steal and shrugs off the rest. Nearly
all of them crave machine parts, and most have traded their invisibility for a
bionic arm or a built-in weapon.

## GM Notes

The book offers the Brodkil as a villain first and a player character only at
the G.M.''s option. Its stat block reads like an NPC''s: five attacks and the
listed bonuses may already count the hand to hand, boxing and wrestling it
lists, so decide whether those stack before play.

Bionics are always partial, never a full conversion, and any bionic weapon or
implant ends the ability to turn invisible. The 3D6 M.D. power punch belongs to
a bionic arm. Typical kit is a heavy energy rifle, optics, a magic weapon when
one can be stolen and now and then a hover vehicle; none of it is issued, so
the character starts with what the G.M. allows. Extra skills, if any, come from
Weapon Proficiencies, Communications, Technical, Domestic and Wilderness
without bonuses.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'brodkil');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'brodkil';

